-- title:
--   Component labels on the crossing charts match the toric table
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a package $\mathfrak{X}$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data for level $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Assume the bundle [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) (finiteness of the node set $\mathrm{Node} = \mathrm{pullback}(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa, \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa)$, existence of oriented crossing charts, the étale-neighbourhood property, injectivity and closedness of the node points, and the model hypotheses on the toric resolutions), summarised here, together with `hξ`, saying that both auxiliary points $\xi_j$ lie in the open locus $X_0$ of the associated chart input [`V3Asm.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L280). Assume further given, for every $e$, a family $Fc\,e : \mathrm{Fin}(e+1) \to$ ideal sheaf data on the toric resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}(p,e)$ satisfying the chart table: pulling $Fc\,e\,k$ back along the $i$-th chart $\iota$ yields the ideal sheaf generated by $V$ when $k=i$, by $U$ when $k=i+1$, and the unit ideal otherwise, the generators transported from $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,O\,p$ by the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`. The conclusion: for every node $n$ and every chain position $d \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}\,n+1)$, the component ideal sheaf $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}(\mathrm{width},n,d))$ on the glued model, restricted to the open $\mathrm{toDR}^{-1}(U_n)$, equals the pullback of $Fc\,(\mathrm{width}\,n)\,d$ along the inverse of the chart isomorphism `chartIso` followed by $g_n$. Here $\mathrm{chainPos}$ sends $d=0$ to the first global component, $0<d<\mathrm{width}\,n$ to the $(d-1)$-st exceptional line above $n$, and $d \ge \mathrm{width}\,n$ to the second global component.
--
--   This is the labelling compatibility field in the construction of a resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over $O$: it identifies the chain of components of the special fibre over each crossing chart with the canonical chain of divisors on the toric resolution of $xy = p$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts) to produce the resolved model together with its étale crossing charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3Asm_label.lean

